   "html": "<h2>What it is</h2>\n<p>A metal that has been used as money for thousands of years. Physical gold is a <strong>bearer asset</strong>: whoever holds it owns it, and no one owes it to you. Central banks still hold large gold reserves alongside their own currencies.</p>\n<h2>Why it exists as money</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Scarce and hard to produce.</strong> New supply each year is small next to the existing stock.</li>\n<li><strong>Durable and uniform.</strong> It doesn't rot or rust, and one ounce is the same as another.</li>\n<li><strong>Nobody's liability.</strong> It can't default, and it doesn't depend on any issuer staying solvent.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How you can hold it</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Form</th>\n<th>What you own</th>\n<th>Whose risk?</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Coins or bars in your possession</td>\n<td>The metal</td>\n<td>Yours: theft, loss, storage</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Allocated vault storage</td>\n<td>Specific bars held for you</td>\n<td>The vault operator's honesty and safety</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Gold ETF or fund</td>\n<td>Shares in a fund that holds gold</td>\n<td>The fund and your broker: this is a claim, not the metal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Gold futures</td>\n<td>A contract</td>\n<td>The exchange and your counterparty</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Physical gold sits in <strong>Tier 2</strong> of the <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/cartography-of-wealth\" data-page=\"cartography-of-wealth\">Cartography of Wealth</a>: private and beyond easy reach of the state, but exposed to theft and your own mistakes. Paper forms (ETFs, futures) are claims and sit with other legible assets in <strong>Tier 3</strong>.</p>\n<h2>What goes wrong</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Theft.</strong> A bearer asset has no recourse desk.</li>\n<li><strong>Confiscation.</strong> In 1933 the United States required citizens to hand in most private gold holdings.</li>\n<li><strong>No yield.</strong> Gold pays nothing while you hold it, and storage costs money.</li>\n<li><strong>Long flat periods.</strong> Gold has gone many years without rising in real terms.</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Key rule:</strong> \"gold\" on a broker statement and gold in a safe are different assets with different killers.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2>Related</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>As an industrial and traded commodity, see <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/commodities\" data-page=\"commodities\">Commodities</a>.</li>\n<li>For its place in the layers of money, see <a class=\"wl\" href=\"#/map/p/hierarchy-of-money\" data-page=\"hierarchy-of-money\">The Hierarchy of Money</a>.</li>\n</ul>",
